{{also|ass backwards}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{qualifier|alternative spelling}} [[ass backwards]], [[ass-backward]], [[ass backward]]
* {{l|en|back-asswards}}, {{l|en|bass-ackwards}}

===Etymology===
Recorded in the US in the 1930s. From {{compound|en|ass|backwards}}<ref>{{cite-book|author=Robert Whitcomb|title=Talk United States!|year=1935|page=145}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-ass-backwards.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} Oriented [[backwards]], particularly after a [[mishap]].
#: {{ux|en|The car spun out of control and I ended up '''ass-backwards''' in a ditch.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|colloquial}} Hopelessly [[misguided]]; contrary to what is normal, expected, or logical; having taken the utterly wrong choice.
#: {{ux|en|No wonder it doesn't work. The whole design is '''ass-backwards'''.}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} Moving backwards, that is, [[rear end]] first.
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|colloquial}} In a hopelessly misguided manner; in a manner contrary to what is normal, expected, or logical.
#: {{ux|en|They did the whole design '''ass-backwards'''. No wonder it doesn't work.}}

